tool_input.content:
%
% bullet_ammo.tex
%
% Z Specification for the XBoing bullet/ammo subsystem
% Formal model of the authoritative ammo count, the ammo-belt UI display,
% and the end-of-level bullet bonus — built to expose a display/bonus
% desync bug in the unlimited-ammo (MAXAMMO) path.
%

\documentclass[a4paper,10pt,fleqn]{article}
\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}
\usepackage{fuzz}
\usepackage[colorlinks=true,linkcolor=blue,citecolor=blue,urlcolor=blue]{hyperref}

\begin{document}

\title{XBoing Bullet/Ammo: A Z Specification}
\author{Formal Model of the Ammo Count, Belt Display, and Bullet Bonus}
\date{July 2026}
\hypersetup{
  pdftitle={XBoing Bullet/Ammo: A Z Specification},
  pdfauthor={xboing-c},
  pdfsubject={Z Specification},
  pdfcreator={fuzz/probcli}
}
\maketitle

\tableofcontents
\newpage

\section{Introduction}

This is a narrow model of the bullet/ammo subsystem, built to locate a
reported desync: the player fired bullets while the ammo belt showed
none, and the end-of-level bonus rewarded many bullets the player did
not appear to hold.

The model separates three quantities the code keeps distinct:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{actualAmmo} --- the authoritative count owned by
      \texttt{gun\_system} (\texttt{gun\_system\_get\_ammo}).
\item \textbf{displayedAmmo} --- how many bullets the ammo-belt renderer
      draws in the HUD (\texttt{game\_render\_ammo\_belt}).
\item \textbf{bonusAmmo} --- the count the end-of-level bonus reads and
      rewards (\texttt{mode\_bonus\_enter} $\to$
      \texttt{bonus\_system}).
\end{itemize}

The MAXAMMO block sets \texttt{unlimited} and stores a sentinel count of
\texttt{GUN\_MAX\_AMMO + 1}.  The renderer hides the belt entirely when
\texttt{unlimited} is set; the bonus reads the raw sentinel.  The
property \texttt{displayedAmmo = bonusAmmo} --- what you see equals what
you are paid for --- is therefore violated, and this model exhibits the
reachable state that violates it.

\section{Free Types}

\begin{zed}
ZBOOL ::= ztrue | zfalse
\end{zed}

\section{Global Constants}

\begin{axdef}
maxAmmo : \nat \\
ammoPerLevel : \nat \\
bulletsPerPickup : \nat \\
unlimitedSentinel : \nat
\where
maxAmmo = 20 \\
ammoPerLevel = 4 \\
bulletsPerPickup = 4 \\
unlimitedSentinel = maxAmmo + 1
\end{axdef}

\section{Belt Display Function}

The renderer's belt rule as coded: hide the belt when unlimited, else
draw the count capped at the belt width.  \texttt{beltShown} maps
(unlimited, actualAmmo) to the number of bullets the HUD draws.

\begin{axdef}
beltShown : ZBOOL \cross \nat \fun \nat
\where
\forall a : \nat @ beltShown(ztrue, a) = 0 \\
\forall a : \nat @ \\
\quad~ (a \leq maxAmmo \implies beltShown(zfalse, a) = a) \\
\land (a > maxAmmo \implies beltShown(zfalse, a) = maxAmmo)
\end{axdef}

\section{Gun State}

\texttt{displayedAmmo} is a derived rendering of state, pinned by the
belt rule each frame.  \texttt{bonusAmmo} is a snapshot the bonus screen
takes; it is meaningful only once \texttt{inBonus} is set.

\begin{schema}{Gun}
actualAmmo : \nat \\
unlimited : ZBOOL \\
displayedAmmo : \nat \\
inBonus : ZBOOL \\
bonusAmmo : \nat
\where
actualAmmo \leq unlimitedSentinel \\
bonusAmmo \leq unlimitedSentinel \\
displayedAmmo = beltShown(unlimited, actualAmmo) \\
(unlimited = zfalse \implies actualAmmo \leq maxAmmo)
\end{schema}

\begin{schema}{Init}
Gun'
\where
actualAmmo' = ammoPerLevel \\
unlimited' = zfalse \\
displayedAmmo' = ammoPerLevel \\
inBonus' = zfalse \\
bonusAmmo' = 0
\end{schema}

\section{Operations}

\subsection{Fire a bullet}

Guard: ammo available or unlimited.  Unlimited does not decrement
(\texttt{gun\_system\_use\_ammo} is a no-op when unlimited).

\begin{schema}{FireBullet}
\Delta Gun
\where
(actualAmmo > 0 \lor unlimited = ztrue) \\
\land (unlimited = ztrue \implies actualAmmo' = actualAmmo) \\
\land (unlimited = zfalse \implies actualAmmo' = actualAmmo - 1) \\
unlimited' = unlimited \\
inBonus' = inBonus \\
bonusAmmo' = bonusAmmo
\end{schema}

\subsection{Pick up a BULLET block (+4 ammo)}

Ignored when unlimited (matches \texttt{game\_callbacks.c}: the +4 loop
is skipped under unlimited).  Clamps at \texttt{maxAmmo}.

\begin{schema}{PickupBullets}
\Delta Gun
\where
unlimited = zfalse \\
\land (actualAmmo + bulletsPerPickup \leq maxAmmo \\
\quad~ \implies actualAmmo' = actualAmmo + bulletsPerPickup) \\
\land (actualAmmo + bulletsPerPickup > maxAmmo \\
\quad~ \implies actualAmmo' = maxAmmo) \\
unlimited' = unlimited \\
inBonus' = inBonus \\
bonusAmmo' = bonusAmmo
\end{schema}

\subsection{Pick up a MAXAMMO block (unlimited)}

Sets unlimited and stores the sentinel count.  The belt rule then forces
\texttt{displayedAmmo} to 0 --- the belt vanishes.

\begin{schema}{PickupMaxAmmo}
\Delta Gun
\where
actualAmmo' = unlimitedSentinel \\
unlimited' = ztrue \\
inBonus' = inBonus \\
bonusAmmo' = bonusAmmo
\end{schema}

\subsection{Enter the bonus screen}

The bonus reads the raw authoritative count --- no unlimited check, no
cap (\texttt{mode\_bonus\_enter}: \texttt{ammo = gun\_system\_get\_ammo};
\texttt{.bullet\_count = ammo}).

\begin{schema}{EnterBonus}
\Delta Gun
\where
inBonus = zfalse \\
inBonus' = ztrue \\
bonusAmmo' = actualAmmo \\
actualAmmo' = actualAmmo \\
unlimited' = unlimited
\end{schema}

\subsection{Advance to the next level}

Resets unlimited and grants the per-level ammo
(\texttt{game\_rules.c}: \texttt{set\_unlimited(0)};
\texttt{set\_ammo(ammoPerLevel)}).

\begin{schema}{NextLevel}
\Delta Gun
\where
actualAmmo' = ammoPerLevel \\
unlimited' = zfalse \\
inBonus' = zfalse \\
bonusAmmo' = 0
\end{schema}

\section{Consistency Properties}

\subsection{Display matches bonus}

What the player sees on the belt must equal what the bonus rewards.
This is the property the reported bug violates.

\begin{schema}{DisplayMatchesBonus}
Gun
\where
inBonus = ztrue \implies displayedAmmo = bonusAmmo
\end{schema}

\subsection{Bonus never exceeds what was shown}

A weaker, still-violated property: the bonus must not reward more
bullets than the belt ever displayed.

\begin{schema}{BonusNotAboveDisplay}
Gun
\where
inBonus = ztrue \implies bonusAmmo \leq displayedAmmo
\end{schema}

\subsection{Fireability is visible}

If the player can fire, the belt should show at least one bullet.  Under
unlimited, \texttt{displayedAmmo = 0} yet firing is allowed --- so this
too is violated, which is exactly ``firing bullets when it did not look
like I had any''.

\begin{schema}{FireabilityVisible}
Gun
\where
(actualAmmo > 0 \lor unlimited = ztrue) \implies displayedAmmo > 0
\end{schema}

\section{The Violating Trace}

From \texttt{Init}, the sequence

\begin{zed}
Init \semi PickupMaxAmmo \semi EnterBonus
\end{zed}

reaches the state

\begin{zed}
actualAmmo = 21 \land unlimited = ztrue \land displayedAmmo = 0 \\
\land inBonus = ztrue \land bonusAmmo = 21
\end{zed}

which violates \texttt{DisplayMatchesBonus} ($0 \neq 21$),
\texttt{BonusNotAboveDisplay} ($21 \not\leq 0$), and (already after
\texttt{PickupMaxAmmo}) \texttt{FireabilityVisible}
($unlimited = ztrue$ yet $displayedAmmo = 0$).

\section{System Invariants}

\begin{itemize}
\item Physical: $actualAmmo \leq unlimitedSentinel$; the belt rule pins
      $displayedAmmo = beltShown(unlimited, actualAmmo)$.
\item Desired (violated): $inBonus = ztrue \implies displayedAmmo =
      bonusAmmo$.
\item Root cause: three consumers interpret \texttt{unlimited}
      differently.  The belt hides on unlimited (shows 0); firing treats
      unlimited as ``always allowed''; the bonus ignores unlimited and
      reads the raw sentinel.  The fix must make the belt reflect the
      count the bonus rewards (original \texttt{ReDrawBulletsLeft} draws
      the raw count with no unlimited check), restoring a single
      interpretation.
\end{itemize}

\end{document}

