if (!bp->exploding || bp->explode_next_frame != frame)
{
    continue;
}
```
Ball-hit explosions work because they're armed AND checked within the same tick (same `frame`). But the cheat arms explosions via `block_system_explode` from `game_input_global` (src/game_input.c:298), which reads `frame = sdl2_state_frame` ONCE per visual frame BEFORE the per-tick `mode_game_update` runs. By the time `update_explosions` runs inside the tick, the frame counter has advanced, so `explode_next_frame == frame` never holds for the cheat's blocks → they stay stuck exploding forever → `ctx->blocks_exploding` never drains → `block_system_still_active` keeps returning nonzero (its `blocks_exploding > 1` guard) → `game_rules_check` never transitions to SDL2ST_BONUS.

## The fix
Change the gate at src/block_system.c:574 from exact-equality to due-or-past:
```c
if (!bp->exploding || frame < bp->explode_next_frame)
{
    continue;
}
```
i.e. advance the explosion when `frame >= bp->explode_next_frame`. This is the SAME adaptation ADR-070 made for the roamer/drop/random movement timers (`==` → `>=`): robust to an explosion armed on the input path but checked on a later tick, and to skipped frames under the fixed-timestep loop. Each advance still does exactly `explode_slide++; explode_next_frame += BLOCK_EXPLODE_DELAY;` — so it advances AT MOST ONE stage per update_explosions call (no double-advance, no double-score). Verify that: a block armed at F still finalizes one stage per subsequent tick and blocks_exploding decrements to 0.

